## Plan

_Written by `claude-3` (claude, `sonnet`, medium) ([run](https://github.com/Jlore-Studios/JackiOh/actions/runs/44842091520)) before anyone built this. The night bot's builder starts from this section: edit it here to change the plan._

**Goal.** At 744×1133 the deck builder's "Compare with" picker shows its label and its chosen option ("Another deck or a trio…") in full, and the editor has no horizontal overflow. The layouts at 820×1180, 390×844 and the desktop sizes are unchanged. A spec 46 check fails on the clipped picker. The fix is CSS only, plus the proof and a ruling note.

**Cause (measured in headless Chromium with the shipped Inter font).**
- At 744 the sidebar is 232 px, so 210 px inside.
- `workshop.css`'s `@media (max-width: 760px)` block puts the label beside the select and sets the select to 16 px. The select is then about 104 px wide, against 178.5 px of text.
- Stacking the label alone is not enough. 16 px text needs a select about 218 px wide (it is cut at 214), and only 210 px is available.
- At 13 px, the body size and what 820 already uses, the text is 145 px and fits with room to spare.
- A native select's `scrollWidth` never reports clipped text, so the check must measure the text itself.

